From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:27:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] autotests: A declared X11 child is shown only where X
 shows it

testStereoChildWindowClip: a child larger than its window is cut to the window;
a sibling stacked over it is cut out, comes back when it is unmapped and goes
again when it is mapped; a sibling that appears after the child was listed, moves
and is destroyed; the child raised over the sibling is not covered and lowered
under it is again; a sibling with a bounding shape covers only its bars, and
follows a change of its shape; the quads of both eyes cover the child's views
only where it is shown. testStereoChildWindowClipAncestor: a child inside a
window of its own is cut to that window and to a sibling of that window stacked
over it, and follows the window's move. Both fail without the change (visible
stays empty; without the cut in shapeForSourceBox() the quads cover the whole
200x150 child).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 autotests/integration/x11_window_test.cpp | 189 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 189 insertions(+)

diff --git a/autotests/integration/x11_window_test.cpp b/autotests/integration/x11_window_test.cpp
index dfa986f00c..5f6eef84a0 100644
--- a/autotests/integration/x11_window_test.cpp
+++ b/autotests/integration/x11_window_test.cpp
@@ -163,6 +163,8 @@ private Q_SLOTS:
     void testStereoChildWindowListedBeforeMapping();
